      "dom_id": "question-5446",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "An arithmetic series has the first term ${a}_{1}=4$, the $8$th term ${a}_{8}=60$, and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=1600.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series.",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{8}-{a}_{1}}{8-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{60-4}{8-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{56}{7} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=4$, $d=8$, and ${S}_{N}=1600$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 1600 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2\\cdot 4+(N-1)\\cdot 8) \\\\ 1600 & =\\frac{N}{2}(8+8N-8) \\\\ 1600 & =\\frac{N}{2}(8N) \\\\ 1600 & =4{N}^{2} \\\\ 400 & ={N}^{2} \\\\ N & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because $N$ can't be negative.",
